LogNextChar 1.4.0
- Next and Prev show the slot they log into, big under their name in cyan (playing slot 4: Next 5, Prev 3).
- A Modern look, now the default: flat dark panels with a thin border, cyan for the selection, gold for the main button, Cherry's Bar's icons. Gold on the character screen sits beside a coin, with charges and the last save under it; the character, channel and server lists fit what is in them; server rows show the flag and your character count beside a helmet; the settings toggles are grouped under headings. Buttons, check boxes, edit boxes, lists and the character creation sliders match.
- "Modern look", the first toggle in the settings panel, switches to the game's own look (Classic) and back at once, without a reload. config.lua: modern_ui = false.
- The textures are in media/, drawn by tools/build_login_skin.py; template/skin.lua holds both looks.
- Fixed: Tab moves between the two boxes of a dialog that asks for two entries (its script didn't compile).

LogNextChar 1.3.3
- Next and Prev wait for the whole character list before picking, start from the character left by name, and hold the pick until the login starts, so the game's own late selection can't leave you on the character screen.
- A cancelled logout drops the queued switch in game.

LogNextChar 1.3.2
- The character screen shows Arcane Transmutor charges under gold, as Charges: #, from Global Bank's data.

LogNextChar 1.3.1
- The character screen finds a character's gold by server and name, so characters with the same name on different servers no longer show each other's gold. Gold saved before servers were recorded shows a ?.

LogNextChar 1.3.0
- Cherry's Loginxml and LogNextChar are now one addon, LogNextChar, in Interface\AddOns\CherrysKit\LogNextChar. The installer removes the old CherrysLoginxmlHook folder, and your saved logins and toggles stay.

Cherry's Loginxml 1.2.2
- the in-game addon is now Interface\AddOns\CherrysKit\CherrysLoginxmlHook. The installer removes the old Interface\AddOns\CherrysLoginxml folder.

Cherry's Loginxml 1.2.1
- The character screen shows each character's gold and when it was last saved, from Global Bank's data. The server screen says when Global Bank's helper isn't running or hasn't been set up.

Cherry's Loginxml 1.2.0
Original project: Rom Autologin by Pyrrhus. Integration fixes by Cherry.
- new name: Cherry's Loginxml, shown next to the client version on the login screen
- server screen: toggle buttons for every on/off setting, to the right of the server list; a click applies at once
- new setting character_login_first: log in the first character once after each account login
- settings changed on the login screen are kept by the new CherrysLoginxml addon (Interface\AddOns), which the game saves when you log out or quit; "Use config.lua" forgets them
- new Install login screen.bat in the addon's folder: one click copies the login screen to Interface\loginxml, keeps your own files, and stores the path to SaveVariables.lua so toggles are back after a restart
- in game, the addon says in chat when the login screen is missing or a different version
- a row in the Cherry's Kit hub
- added frames/compat_stock.lua: recreates the CHARACTER_SELECT global (selectedIndex) that the default login screen provides
- server and character lists: Up/Down arrow keys move the selection, Enter joins / logs in
- launcher logins: the Retry button counts down and asks for the server list again on its own
  (config server_list_retry = 10 seconds, 0 = by hand only; server_list_retry_max = 3)
- DEBUG button only shows when debug = true
- CampNext (works with LogNextChar): "current" and "index" modes, 15s timeout, armable from the DEBUG box (campnext next|prev|current|<slot>|cancel)
- CampNext: clicking a character or using the arrow keys cancels a queued switch; automatic logins wait for a queued switch
- CampNext: leaves the character names in LOGCHAR_ROSTER so LogNextChar can name the next character in game

v1.1.0
- added CampNext_Login to integrate functionality with LogNextChar.lua
